System Architecture & Storefront Strategy Document
Target Audience: Agentic Development Team / System Engineers
1. Executive Summary & Core Value Proposition

This document outlines the architectural and market strategy for a premium Action RPG (ARPG) Roguelike built in Godot utilizing Synty assets. The core mechanical hook is "Keep What You Kill"—a necromantic lifecycle where players reincarnate into the character kits of defeated enemy bosses.
The game’s content matrix is entirely driven by a pre-runtime data-science pipeline that data-mines 25 years of canonical ARPG history. Development velocity is optimized by decoupling data-generation from runtime rule-sets. This allows for the rapid deployment of free, nostalgic custom mini-games (inspired by Warcraft 3 and StarCraft) inside a unified Steam application wrapper to aggressively harvest wishlists and drive community acquisition without video-marketing overhead.
2. Technical Architecture Pipeline

The system utilizes an iterative, automated manufacturing loop executed completely prior to runtime. The application client operates strictly on serialized static data packages, eliminating live external network dependencies during execution.
