Phase 1: The Scraping & Taxonomy Matrix (The Periodic Table)

Source Data: Aggregated, crowd-sourced community wikis, build guides, and balance patch histories spanning 15 canonical ARPG titles over a 25-year timeline.
The Cell Matrix: Mechanical data points are filtered down to structural coordinates representing periods where specific builds achieved historical stabilization.
The Skill Spine: Each cell contains a custom skill tree "spine" that isolates the single most representative mechanical variation out of hundreds of hidden permutations.
Phase 2: Pre-Runtime Compilation

Weapon Selection: The script assigns a historical or fictional weapon base profile.
Cell Mapping: The character is matched to a specific mechanical cell coordinate from the Periodic Table.
Headless Simulation: The script runs multi-thousand-cycle automated combat simulations at 100x execution speeds to test pacing metrics (Time-to-Kill, resource curves, survival rates per zone).
LLM Text Synthesis: The local tool makes structured pre-runtime API calls to generate theme-appropriate nomenclature (elemental titles, flavor text, race, and faction associations).
3D Asset Binding: The script maps the output parameters directly to localized Godot 3D engine meshes and Synty Asset library IDs.
Serialization: The pipeline outputs a complete, finalized JSON character/boss profile prior to application runtime.
