4. Mini-Game Deployment Strategy (Rapid-Fire Content)

Because the character kits, statistics, and asset configurations are pre-validated by the data science pipeline, game modes are reduced to lightweight rule-set wrappers. This structure enables a high-velocity, bi-weekly deployment cycle.
Rule-Set Wrapper Execution Priorities

Low Friction Modules (Estimated 1-2 Weeks Execution):
Hero Line Wars / Horde Defense: Direct translation of existing ARPG top-down movement and combat matrices. Requires basic lane divider rules, spawn wave timers, and path-finding aggro behaviors.
Medium Friction Modules (Estimated 3-4 Weeks Execution):
Tower Defense / Auto Chess: Requires secondary structural layers including placement grids, automatic node-based targeting, static attack behaviors, and basic draft phase mechanics. The underlying combat, damage, and stat scaling math remains untouched.
The Lore Integration Bridge

The mini-games are contextually framed as "Tactical Soul Simulations" or "Memory Re-enactments." The player uses the exact same data-generated JSON profiles to pilot characters in the mini-games as they do when encountering them as bosses or player configurations in the main 25-minute, 3-zone Roguelike game loop (Dungeon → Biome → Escape).
5. Valve AI Compliance Framework

The application pipeline is architected to clear Steamworks review without encountering strict auditing bottlenecks.
