6. Marketing Execution (The Non-Video Text Strategy)

This strategy bypasses traditional face-cam video marketing and content creation, shifting all energy toward high-density written technical logs targeting analytical communities (Hacker News, r/Godot, r/gamedev, and hardcore ARPG forums).
The Chronological Taxonomy Hack (Legal & Marketing Shield)

To capture maximum player nostalgia without violating corporate trademark laws via proprietary class names (e.g., Witch Doctor or Sorceress), the public-facing Periodic Table labels cells by factual chronological metadata.
Formula: [Game Identifier] - [Release Year] - [Patch Version] + [Mechanical Description]
Example Cell: D2-2001 (v1.09) Splintering Ice Radial
Example Cell: D3-2012 (v1.0.4) Flame-Echo Summoner
Strategic Benefits:

Legal Air Gap: Stating historical, factual patch markers is protected under nominative fair use. It bypasses corporate keyword scanners and automated Steam DMCA filters.
Cunningham’s Law Engagement: Hardcore min-maxers remember game eras perfectly. Presenting the cells as scientific historical data points challenges veterans to audit the search space, naturally driving them into your community hub to argue, test, and provide high-value alpha feedback.
